diff --git a/prompts/LEARNINGS.md b/prompts/LEARNINGS.md
index 9f04e688f..ed00ff2ed 100644
--- a/prompts/LEARNINGS.md
+++ b/prompts/LEARNINGS.md
@@ -1839,6 +1839,12 @@
 - **Adapted:** spare `is_idle_task(t)` (all CPUs) + `is_current_on_any_cpu(t)` in the loop, mirroring `terminate_err`'s remote-current refusal and `cleanup_test_tasks`' spare set. Gates: x86_64 release 24/24 (was 23/24), aarch64 release 28/28, riscv64 release 35/35, debug smp 21/21.
 - **Style re-face:** every teardown path must check any-CPU currency, not just local current — `reap_orphans` still only spares calling-CPU `current` (its callers happen to be safe today); audit any new caller against `is_current_on_any_cpu` before wiring it up.
 
+### #522 — aarch64 scheduler_idle hang: unregistered task enqueued + unconditional epilogue apply (FIXED, gates green)
+
+- **Learned:** (1) QMP stop + info registers beats GDB batch for TCG stalls (batch `continue &` + `interrupt` never stops the target; QMP gives PC/PSTATE in seconds). PC in `forever_entry` + PSTATE I-bit CLEAR (0x345 has I=0 — decode the bits, don't assume masked) ruled out the masked-scan theory and proved live ticks with a scheduler that always no-ops. (2) The full chain: `set_current` re-enqueued READY-but-unregistered `t` via `enqueue_ready_inner` (which bypasses `enqueue_ready`'s H2 ownership guard) → tick picked it via the state-unchecked EDF return in `next_task` → `switch_to_task` armed (state READY passes its gate) → aarch64 epilogue applied unconditionally (no `scheduler_validate_pending_switch`, unlike x86/riscv) → CPU ran `t` while books said current=harness → every later tick picked harness, `switch_to_task(harness,harness)` early-returned, epilogue found nothing armed — silence forever. x86/riscv survive via the validator abort + drop_arm re-queue. (3) `[[nodiscard]]`-style discipline applies to asm too: the file's own comment documented the missing validation as an "audited S3 limitation" — a documented gap on the scheduler-critical path is a deferred hang, not a limitation.
+- **Adapted:** `set_current` refuses to link TCBs `find_task(old->id) != old` (mirrors the H2 guard; harness/AP-idles are registered so no behavior change for owned tasks — verified by audit of all `set_current` callers); aarch64 `irq_context_switch_common` calls the shared validator + `scheduler_abort_switch_fixup` on abort, aborting to `.restore` with SP untouched (C-call safe: frame holds all user state, x0/x1 reloaded, LR dead, SP aligned).
+- **Style re-face:** when the books (current=harness) and the CPU (running t) disagree, suspect the apply path, not the pick logic — the pick was legal-ish, the apply was unchecked; parity gaps documented in comments («unlike x86…») are bugs with a serial number — close them in the same cycle as the trigger fix; QMP-first for all future TCG stall captures.
+
 ### #523 — aarch64 pager tests: no delegation (hang) + trap kill skipped release_zombie (PMM+45 leak) (FIXED, gates green)
 
 - **Learned:** (1) The only production `delegate_fault` call site was x86 (`kernel.cpp:2573`) — aarch64/riscv64 EL0/U-mode fault handlers killed unconditionally, so pager probes SIGSEGV'd before delegating: `pending_fault` never true → assert FAIL → leaked TERMINATED probe → next test's `drive_until(pending)` spun forever (STALL). One missing hook explained FAIL + leak + hang. (2) The fault-kill shape (`TERMINATED` + wake + `switch_away`) skipped `release_zombie`, so `terminate_and_drain` on an already-TERMINATED task just drained an empty zombie list — PMM+45/Tasks+1/MQ+1 leaked per fault-killed task on aa64/rv64 while x86 (full `terminate_err` via signal delivery) stayed clean. Fix is the shared `terminate_err_from_trap` prefix (dequeue + join-note + wake + `release_zombie` + reaper poke, NO `switch_to_task`) called before the existing deferred switch — zombie-before-arm order is load-bearing. (3) `[[nodiscard]]` + `-Werror=unused-result` forces consuming the helper's return even when refusal is impossible — capture + `(void)` with the reason. (4) Parity work exposes latent arch bugs: riscv64 probe VA 0x10000000 aliases the UART identity window (test-6 assert premise wrong, same class as #352) and split-L2 pages leak on teardown (riscv64-only) — both filed as follow-ups (#526/#527), not fixed in the pager change.
diff --git a/src/kernel/arch/aarch64/vectors.S b/src/kernel/arch/aarch64/vectors.S
index 24fb47a0d..41fe3f447 100644
--- a/src/kernel/arch/aarch64/vectors.S
+++ b/src/kernel/arch/aarch64/vectors.S
@@ -256,6 +256,8 @@ el0_sync:
 
 .extern scheduler_save_rsp_to
 .extern scheduler_load_rsp_from
+.extern scheduler_validate_pending_switch
+.extern scheduler_abort_switch_fixup
 .extern scheduler_load_cr3_from
 .extern scheduler_load_tls_from // Issue #74: TLS base publish slot
 .extern scheduler_on_context_switch
@@ -287,10 +289,14 @@ el0_irq:
     // fall through to irq_context_switch_common
 
 // After handle_gic_irq, check for scheduler context switch
-// NOTE (audited limitation, S3): unlike the x86_64 isr_stubs epilogue this
-// path performs no deferred-switch generation re-check, no isr-nesting
-// depth guard and no H2 liveness/ownership re-validation — the arm is
-// applied as observed.  Documented follow-up for the aarch64 H2 port.
+// Issue #522: this path now performs the deferred-switch liveness +
+// ownership re-check (scheduler_validate_pending_switch), mirroring the
+// x86_64 isr_stubs and riscv64 syscall_entry epilogues — the arm can
+// outlive its tick and the target can be removed/never-registered in
+// between (resuming an unregistered task with DAIF masked stalled
+// scheduler_idle silently).  Generation re-check + ISR-nesting-depth
+// guard remain a tracked follow-up (single-CPU + IRQs masked here, so a
+// torn publish is impossible today).
 .globl irq_context_switch_common
 .type irq_context_switch_common, @function
 irq_context_switch_common:
@@ -302,6 +308,16 @@ irq_context_switch_common:
     mov     x1, sp
     str     x1, [x0]
 
+    // H2 apply-side liveness + ownership re-check.  C call with the trap
+    // frame intact: every user GPR is in the save area (save_all ran
+    // above); x0/x1 are scratch here (reloaded via adrp after the call)
+    // and LR is dead (clobbered by the handle_gic_irq bl above; the
+    // epilogue ends in eret, never ret).  SP stays 16-byte aligned.
+    // Returns 1 = apply, 0 = abort (validator cleared the atoms and
+    // undid the publish side effects).
+    bl      scheduler_validate_pending_switch
+    cbz     w0, .Lswitch_abort
+
     // Load new SP from scheduler_load_rsp_from
     adrp    x1, scheduler_load_rsp_from
     ldr     x1, [x1, #:lo12:scheduler_load_rsp_from]
@@ -350,6 +366,15 @@ irq_context_switch_common:
     adrp    x4, scheduler_load_tls_from
     str     xzr, [x4, #:lo12:scheduler_load_tls_from]
 8:  isb
+    b       .restore
+
+.Lswitch_abort:
+    // The validator refused the arm (removed/unregistered target or
+    // foreign RSP) and already invalidated the atoms + undid the publish
+    // side effects.  Rebind arm-side redirects, then resume the
+    // interrupted task (SP untouched — the new SP was never loaded).
+    bl      scheduler_abort_switch_fixup
+    b       .restore
 
 .restore:
     restore_all
diff --git a/src/kernel/task/scheduler_switch.cpp b/src/kernel/task/scheduler_switch.cpp
index 19ba2e133..2f93d638b 100644
--- a/src/kernel/task/scheduler_switch.cpp
+++ b/src/kernel/task/scheduler_switch.cpp
@@ -267,10 +267,22 @@ void Scheduler::set_current(TaskControlBlock &task) noexcept {
         old->magic == TaskControlBlock::TCB_MAGIC &&
         (old->state == TaskState::READY ||
          old->state == TaskState::RUNNING)) {
-        old->in_ready_queue_ = false;
-        old->rq_priority_ = 0;
-        old->ready_deferred_ = false;
-        enqueue_ready_inner(*old);
+        // Issue #522: ownership guard (mirrors the H2 guard in
+        // enqueue_ready).  The impersonation pattern (ScopedCurrentTask
+        // over an unregistered task) linked the outgoing task here; the
+        // aarch64 epilogue then applied the resulting arm
+        // unconditionally and the CPU resumed an unregistered task with
+        // DAIF masked (silent stall in idle_mem_overhead_bounded).  An
+        // unowned TCB stays current-resumable via set_current_ptr below
+        // but never enters dispatch.
+        if (Scheduler::find_task(old->id) != old) {
+            old->in_ready_queue_ = false;
+        } else {
+            old->in_ready_queue_ = false;
+            old->rq_priority_ = 0;
+            old->ready_deferred_ = false;
+            enqueue_ready_inner(*old);
+        }
     }
 
     set_current_ptr(&task);
